// A bare "_" is the wildcard even when a class named "_" is declared earlier
// in the source, so a declared name never makes it a structural sub-pattern
// of an @-binding: the sub-pattern must be a structural pattern
// (spec/02-syntax.md, armPat and subPat; spec/04-semantics.md, @-bindings;
// issue #762).
class _ {}
enum E { _(x) }

print "never";
var a = match _() { case p @ _ => 1 case _ => 0 };
var b = match E._(7) { case p @ _ => 1 case _ => 0 };

// STATUS: error
// STATIC-ERROR
